<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Psalm 23</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">traditionally ascribed to David; dated by many scholars to after the Babylonian exile</span> · Also known as תהילים כג, Tehillim 23</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Psalm 23 is the 23rd psalm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-psalms">Book of Psalms</a>, part of the third section of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> and a book of the Christian Old Testament; in the numbering of the Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septuagint">Septuagint</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Vulgate it is Psalm 22, known in Latin as &quot;Dominus regit me&quot;. Its heading ascribes it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a>, who in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> Scriptures was a shepherd in his youth.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Psalm 23</b> is the 23rd psalm of the Book of Psalms, part of the third section of the Hebrew Bible and a book of the Christian Old Testament; in the numbering of the Greek Septuagint and the Latin Vulgate it is Psalm 22, known in Latin as &quot;Dominus…</blockquote><a href="/songs/psalm-23">Psalm 23</a></li></ul></section>
